      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T08:14:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TOP_OF_PIPE bit as src doesn\u0027t wait for completion of any operation which may be pending on this resource. I am not sure this is what we want (from a correctness point of view).\nAs we are currently not observing issues by not transferring the resource testing with this patch will also not reveal potential issues.\nFrom my PoV this must include all stages Skia could have used to modify the resource (fragment|transfer ?).",
      "revId": "c56c78c6a624f42b6f157c1561fa0c177eae007a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d4f559f_dea5d9bd",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanTexture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T14:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that when doing a queue transfer from foreign/external to the graphics queue top is the correct thing to use. My understanding is that the src stages are about protecting work between same queue operations. So since this is being imported externally, there is no work on the current queue we need to block on. The same logic applies for why we can use Bottom on the export call. But maybe I am misunderstanding something about the spec.",
      "parentUuid": "74a7b1f4_156348d5",
      "revId": "c56c78c6a624f42b6f157c1561fa0c177eae007a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42825f87_3557171b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanTexture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 3405028
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T14:54:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does Skia guarantee no work is pending in this (or another) queue? Then TOP is fine, yes.",
      "parentUuid": "2d4f559f_dea5d9bd",
      "revId": "c56c78c6a624f42b6f157c1561fa0c177eae007a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70c281cc_44ec1660",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanTexture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T15:07:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the past Skia has only use one queue but Nathan has been moving to a place we can use both a protected and unprotected queue inside Skia if needed. So he would be the best to answer the multiple queue part of the question. When we\u0027re just dealing with one queue I think in \"normal\" expected use this should be fine because someone importing this from foreign should be synchronizing things with semaphores and such (access masks are still all get set so memory availablity/visibility should be fine). However, I\u0027m trying to think through a scenario where some first exports to foreign from Skia after drawing to a VkImage, so `srcStage \u003d COLOR_WRITE and dstStage \u003d BOTTOM`. Then they just immediately import it back to Skia\u0027s graphics queue without doing anything outside Skia and want to be use it for sampling in a shader, so `srcStage \u003d TOP and dstStage \u003d SHADER_READ`. Would those barriers be able to protect the RAW hazard?",
      "parentUuid": "42825f87_3557171b",
      "revId": "c56c78c6a624f42b6f157c1561fa0c177eae007a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
